<section class="section field" aria-labelledby="h-field">
  <div class="wrap field">
    <div>
      <h2 id="h-field">Research alone doesn't shift power.</h2>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem">So we pair open research with civic-tech prototypes, run them with real partners and communities, and feed what we learn back into policy proposals and further pilots. That's the civic muscle participatory governance actually requires, and it's built in public: through our Salons and podcast, through papers and proposals like the <a href="/projects/the-plural-stack">Plural Stack</a> and <a href="https://youtu.be/OZqXrjwF3nE">Reverse Alignment</a>, and through a global community that tests these ideas in its own cities.</p>
      <a class="more" href="/about/">About the Foundation, the team and our approach</a>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="board">The Foundation's board includes <b>E. Glen Weyl</b>, <b>Audrey Tang</b>, <b>Vitalik Buterin</b>, <b>Anne-Marie Slaughter</b>, <b>Christopher Kulendran Thomas</b> and <b>Joseph Gordon-Levitt</b>. RadicalxChange grew out of the ideas in <i>Radical Markets</i> and <i>Plurality</i>, and remains the home of the movement those books started.</p>
      <p class="board">Chapters are autonomous and driven by their own local character, from Amsterdam to Auckland, Mexico City to Mumbai. Every chapter operates under our <a href="/community/code-of-conduct/">code of conduct</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

